OL,0,          BTXT64  GSat 21.11.26 22:36:26
OL,1,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,2,FTeletextC64D]FBio                      
OL,3,   EUltimateD]GCommodore x Teletext     
OL,4,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,5,BBio Frank Putman                       
OL,6, I grew up with theFCommodore 64Gas a   
OL,7, teenager in the 1980s and have always  
OL,8, been a big Teletext fan. In the        
OL,9, mid-1980s, I discoveredCthe magic of   
OL,10,Cprogramming computersGand have         
OL,11, continued doing so to this day. I also 
OL,12, had anFAmiga 2000Gbut switched to PC's 
OL,13, like so many of us.                    
OL,15, Professionally, I developed Teletext   
OL,16, software for a Dutch, Delft-based com- 
OL,17, pany in the early 1990s. They developed
OL,18, their own Teletext hardware based      
OL,19, around theFPhilips SAA5243GIC. We were 
OL,20, market leader, with products such asF  
OL,21,FLANtext, WINtext and Wall $treet       
OL,22,FProfessional.GIt was a great adventure!
OL,23,D]F308G<<                >>F310 B]D1/2  
